  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Splines de regresión con funciones base\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objetivos\n",
        "\n",
        "En esta práctica estudiaremos cómo ajustar relaciones no lineales utilizando **splines de regresión**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Trabajaremos nuevamente con el conjunto de datos `Wage`.\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: diapositivas\n",
        "::: diapositivas-title\n",
        "📝 **Diapositivas**\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: diapositivas-body\n",
        "[Ver diapositivas Funciones Base](https://github.com/CursosENESJuriquilla/TS_Aprendizaje_de_Maquina_2027-1/blob/main/Material/2.4_Funciones_Base.pdf)\n",
        "\n",
        "[Ver diapositivas Splines de Regresión](https://github.com/CursosENESJuriquilla/TS_Aprendizaje_de_Maquina_2027-1/blob/main/Material/2.5_Splines_de_regresion.pdf)\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Librerías\n",
        "\n",
        "Comenzamos importando las librerías necesarias."
      ],
      "id": "494845a5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "\n",
        "from ISLP import load_data\n",
        "\n",
        "from ISLP.models import (\n",
        "    ModelSpec as MS,\n",
        "    summarize,\n",
        "    bs,\n",
        "    ns,\n",
        "    poly\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "from ISLP.transforms import (\n",
        "    BSpline,\n",
        "    NaturalSpline\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "e1970534",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Las funciones principales que utilizaremos son:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `BSpline()`: construye directamente una matriz de funciones base B-spline;\n",
        "- `bs()`: permite incluir un B-spline dentro de `ModelSpec`;\n",
        "- `NaturalSpline()`: construye una base para un spline cúbico natural;\n",
        "- `ns()`: permite especificar un spline natural dentro de `ModelSpec`;\n",
        "- `sm.OLS()`: ajusta el modelo lineal una vez construidas las funciones base.\n",
        "\n",
        "Aunque el ajuste final utiliza regresión lineal, la relación entre $X$ y $Y$ puede ser no lineal porque reemplazamos $X$ por funciones transformadas de $X$.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Cargar los datos `Wage`"
      ],
      "id": "ba8331ad"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Wage = load_data(\"Wage\")\n",
        "\n",
        "Wage.head()"
      ],
      "id": "e524d39b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Recordemos algunas de las variables disponibles."
      ],
      "id": "4d3c2d82"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Wage.columns"
      ],
      "id": "666ab5b7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Utilizaremos:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `age`: edad del trabajador;\n",
        "- `wage`: salario."
      ],
      "id": "18459291"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "age = Wage[\"age\"]\n",
        "wage = Wage[\"wage\"]"
      ],
      "id": "aaae3c81",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Veamos algunas estadísticas descriptivas."
      ],
      "id": "d5bbcd61"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Wage[[\"age\", \"wage\"]].describe()"
      ],
      "id": "da237779",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Visualización inicial\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes de ajustar cualquier modelo, observemos los datos."
      ],
      "id": "24abe9ac"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    age,\n",
        "    wage,\n",
        "    alpha=0.25\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Salario\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Salario en función de la edad\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "1d6b36b5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La nube de puntos no sugiere una relación estrictamente lineal.\n",
        "\n",
        "Parece existir una tendencia general:\n",
        "\n",
        "- el salario aumenta durante parte del rango de edades;\n",
        "- posteriormente el crecimiento se estabiliza;\n",
        "- hacia edades mayores puede observarse una disminución.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto motiva el uso de modelos capaces de representar relaciones no lineales.\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Qué es un spline?\n",
        "\n",
        "Un spline cúbico es una función construida mediante distintos polinomios cúbicos definidos en diferentes regiones del predictor.\n",
        "\n",
        "Si tenemos nodos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\xi_1,\\xi_2,\\ldots,\\xi_K,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "estos dividen el rango de $X$ en $K+1$ regiones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Los polinomios se unen imponiendo continuidad de:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$f, f', \\text{ y } f''.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello obtenemos una curva suave incluso en los puntos donde cambia el polinomio.\n",
        "\n",
        "Una representación posible de un spline cúbico es\n",
        "\n",
        "$$f(x)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\beta_0\n",
        "+\\beta_1x\n",
        "+\\beta_2x^2\n",
        "+\\beta_3x^3\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\n",
        "\\beta_{3+k}(x-\\xi_k)_+^3.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Sin embargo, computacionalmente suele ser más conveniente utilizar bases B-spline.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Construir directamente una base B-spline\n",
        "\n",
        "Comencemos colocando tres nodos interiores en\n",
        "\n",
        "$$25,\\qquad 40,\\qquad 60.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizamos `BSpline()`."
      ],
      "id": "de6236a0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bs_transform = BSpline(\n",
        "    internal_knots=[25, 40, 60],\n",
        "    intercept=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "bs_transform"
      ],
      "id": "bb95c26e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Todavía no hemos construido las funciones base.\n",
        "\n",
        "Primero debemos ajustar el transformador al predictor."
      ],
      "id": "7275f3d6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bs_transform = bs_transform.fit(age)"
      ],
      "id": "d1425d82",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora transformamos las edades."
      ],
      "id": "e443f861"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bs_age = bs_transform.transform(age)\n",
        "\n",
        "bs_age"
      ],
      "id": "29aae099",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Veamos sus dimensiones."
      ],
      "id": "a5ce88ae"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bs_age.shape"
      ],
      "id": "8eadac38",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "¿Por qué aparecen **7 columnas**?\n",
        "\n",
        "Tenemos:\n",
        "\n",
        "- un spline cúbico;\n",
        "- $K=3$ nodos interiores;\n",
        "- intercepto incluido.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para un spline cúbico con $K$ nodos tenemos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$K+4$$\n",
        "\n",
        "funciones base.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por tanto,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$3+4=7.$$\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "Si utilizáramos $K=5$ nodos interiores, ¿cuántas columnas tendría la base cúbica incluyendo el intercepto?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip collapse=\"true\" icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## Solución\n",
        "\n",
        "Para un spline cúbico con $K$ nodos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$K+4$$\n",
        "\n",
        "grados de libertad.\n",
        "\n",
        "Si\n",
        "\n",
        "$$K=5,$$\n",
        "\n",
        "entonces:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$5+4=9.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "La matriz tendría **9 columnas**.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Qué representan las columnas de la base?\n",
        "\n",
        "Las columnas de `bs_age` no deben interpretarse como variables originales independientes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Cada columna corresponde a una **función base** evaluada sobre `age`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos visualizar estas funciones. Primero ordenamos las edades, para que las curvas se dibujen de izquierda a derecha:"
      ],
      "id": "a2d22917"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "age_order = np.argsort(age.to_numpy())\n",
        "\n",
        "age_sorted = age.to_numpy()[age_order]"
      ],
      "id": "7cbba616",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Como `bs_age` es un `DataFrame` de pandas, utilizamos `.iloc` para ordenar sus filas:"
      ],
      "id": "7cdffe42"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bs_sorted = bs_age.iloc[age_order, :].to_numpy()"
      ],
      "id": "36b7cfc4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora graficamos cada una de las funciones base:"
      ],
      "id": "557fadef"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "for j in range(bs_sorted.shape[1]):\n",
        "    plt.plot(\n",
        "        age_sorted,\n",
        "        bs_sorted[:, j],\n",
        "        label=f\"Base {j + 1}\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Valor de la función base\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Funciones base B-spline\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "7a0bcacd",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Cada columna de la matriz representa una función\n",
        "\n",
        "$$b_j(x)$$\n",
        "\n",
        "evaluada para todos los valores de `age`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello, la matriz tiene la forma\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "b_1(x_1) & b_2(x_1) & \\cdots & b_p(x_1)\\\\\n",
        "b_1(x_2) & b_2(x_2) & \\cdots & b_p(x_2)\\\\\n",
        "\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n",
        "b_1(x_n) & b_2(x_n) & \\cdots & b_p(x_n)\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Cada función base tiene influencia principalmente sobre una región determinada del dominio.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esta característica permite modificar localmente la forma del ajuste sin alterar drásticamente toda la curva.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Ajustar el spline como un modelo lineal\n",
        "\n",
        "En lugar de construir manualmente la matriz anterior, podemos utilizar `bs()` dentro de `ModelSpec`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos un spline para `age` con los mismos nodos."
      ],
      "id": "ccdd6942"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bs_age_spec = MS([\n",
        "    bs(\n",
        "        \"age\",\n",
        "        internal_knots=[25, 40, 60]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "])"
      ],
      "id": "3187e032",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora ajustamos la especificación a los datos."
      ],
      "id": "bb94eb12"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bs_age_spec = bs_age_spec.fit(Wage)"
      ],
      "id": "1b1a5563",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos la matriz de diseño."
      ],
      "id": "6c14ea2f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_bs = bs_age_spec.transform(Wage)\n",
        "\n",
        "X_bs.head()"
      ],
      "id": "cf86392f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Veamos sus dimensiones."
      ],
      "id": "884ee956"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_bs.shape"
      ],
      "id": "76f1b75f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora ajustamos una regresión lineal."
      ],
      "id": "4f7c5137"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "model_bs = sm.OLS(\n",
        "    wage,\n",
        "    X_bs\n",
        ").fit()"
      ],
      "id": "76f761cb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos resumir el modelo."
      ],
      "id": "db1379f2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "summarize(model_bs)"
      ],
      "id": "19f754b4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## ¿Por qué aparecen menos coeficientes de spline?\n",
        "\n",
        "En el ejemplo anterior `BSpline(..., intercept=True)` produjo 7 columnas.\n",
        "\n",
        "Sin embargo, cuando utilizamos\n",
        "\n",
        "``` python\n",
        "bs(\"age\", internal_knots=[25, 40, 60])\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "dentro de `ModelSpec`, normalmente aparece un intercepto general del modelo y seis términos asociados al spline.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto ocurre porque `bs()` utiliza por defecto\n",
        "\n",
        "``` python\n",
        "intercept=False\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "para evitar introducir redundancia con el intercepto global.\n",
        "\n",
        "Conceptualmente tenemos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\text{intercepto general}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{funciones base del spline}.$$\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Por qué sería problemático introducir dos columnas que representaran exactamente el mismo intercepto?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip collapse=\"true\" icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## Solución\n",
        "\n",
        "Porque las columnas serían linealmente dependientes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto produciría una matriz de diseño que no tiene rango completo y los parámetros no podrían identificarse de manera única.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello, cuando el modelo ya contiene un intercepto general, normalmente la base del spline no incluye otro intercepto independiente.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: callout-note\n",
        "Podemos simplificar los nombres de la tabla como sigue:\n",
        "\n",
        "``` python\n",
        "bs_age_spec = MS([bs('age', internal_knots=[25,40,60], name='bs(age)')])\n",
        "\n",
        "X_bs = bs_age.fit_transform(Wage)\n",
        "\n",
        "model_bs = sm.OLS(wage, X_bs).fit()\n",
        "\n",
        "summarize(model_bs)\n",
        "```\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Predicciones sobre una malla de edades\n",
        "\n",
        "Para visualizar el ajuste construiremos una secuencia de edades."
      ],
      "id": "12cef2ed"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "age_grid = np.linspace(\n",
        "    age.min(),\n",
        "    age.max(),\n",
        "    500\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "6dff95e0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Creamos un `DataFrame` con estas nuevas observaciones."
      ],
      "id": "3da3476d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "age_grid_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"age\": age_grid\n",
        "})"
      ],
      "id": "f29a4383",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora debemos transformar las nuevas edades utilizando **la misma base aprendida con los datos originales**."
      ],
      "id": "3d482071"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_grid_bs = bs_age_spec.transform(age_grid_df)"
      ],
      "id": "c9543c03",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Calculamos las predicciones."
      ],
      "id": "399a7672"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pred_bs = model_bs.get_prediction(X_grid_bs)"
      ],
      "id": "15278e3f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Obtenemos el resumen de predicciones."
      ],
      "id": "856deeb1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pred_bs_summary = pred_bs.summary_frame()\n",
        "\n",
        "pred_bs_summary.head()"
      ],
      "id": "d52408a5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Las columnas incluyen, entre otras:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `mean`: predicción media;\n",
        "- `mean_ci_lower`: límite inferior del intervalo de confianza;\n",
        "- `mean_ci_upper`: límite superior del intervalo de confianza.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Graficar el spline cúbico"
      ],
      "id": "68497952"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    age,\n",
        "    wage,\n",
        "    alpha=0.20\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    age_grid,\n",
        "    pred_bs_summary[\"mean\"],\n",
        "    linewidth=2\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    age_grid,\n",
        "    pred_bs_summary[\"mean_ci_lower\"],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    age_grid,\n",
        "    pred_bs_summary[\"mean_ci_upper\"],\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.axvline(25, linestyle=\":\")\n",
        "plt.axvline(40, linestyle=\":\")\n",
        "plt.axvline(60, linestyle=\":\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Salario\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Spline cúbico con nodos en 25, 40 y 60\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "ed12ae8a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Las líneas verticales indican los nodos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Es importante notar que la curva no presenta saltos en ellos.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inspeccionar los nodos\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos recuperar los nodos utilizados por un objeto `BSpline`."
